  "Caveats": [
    "Much useful logging is off by default: process command lines (4688), scheduled-task events (4698-4702), session reconnects (4778/4779), full script-block logging and file-share access (5140/5145). A missing event proves nothing.",
    "Domain sign-ins are checked by the domain controller, so their Kerberos and NTLM events (4768/4769/4776) are not on this computer.",
    "Logs roll over: each source starts only as far back as its oldest kept record (section 2).",
    "All times are UTC. Clock changes and altered file times can put events in the wrong order.",
    "ShimCache and Amcache show that a file existed, not that it ran; Prefetch shows that a program ran, not what it did.",
    "Private browser windows leave nothing behind, clearing history is not logged, and Chrome does its own DNS lookups.",
    "Email headers can be forged; mailbox and cloud sign-in logs (such as Microsoft 365) are not on this computer.",
    "$MFT file-system rows cover only the 7 days before the collection (-MftDays 7)."
  ],
